  "id": "2122298720955830563",
  "text": "build a painted 3D world in the browser with Opus 5.5 + Three.js,,,\n\nevery frame looks painted, and when the sun goes down it turns from gouache into oil paint\n\nhere’s the workflow:\n\n- step 1: opus 5.5: “plan a walk: forest path > open hill > sunset over the sea”\n- step 2: three.js: opus builds the terrain, path and sea from code, with no models\n- step 3: three.js: procedural trees, grass and flowers with InstancedMesh\n- step 4: three.js: the hero props from basic shapes: blossom tree, floating islands, kid, kite\n- step 5: custom shaders: god rays, fog, birds, fireflies and kite string sway\n- step 6: custom shaders: a paint post-pass that turns every frame into brushstrokes\n- step 7: custom shaders: tie the brush style to sun height: gouache by day, oil at sunset\n- step 8: three.js: a camera path along the walk, with the sun setting as you go\n\nwho does what:\n\n> opus 5.5: writes every mesh, shader and camera move\n> three.js: renders the world\n> the paint shader: makes it look like a painting\n> you: judge each frame like a painting, not a game\nthe brushstrokes hide what code-built shapes can’t fake",
  "raw_text": {
    "text": "build a painted 3D world in the browser with Opus 5.5 + Three.js,,,\n\nevery frame looks painted, and when the sun goes down it turns from gouache into oil paint\n\nhere’s the workflow:\n\n- step 1: opus 5.5: “plan a walk: forest path > open hill > sunset over the sea”\n- step 2: three.js: opus builds the terrain, path and sea from code, with no models\n- step 3: three.js: procedural trees, grass and flowers with InstancedMesh\n- step 4: three.js: the hero props from basic shapes: blossom tree, floating islands, kid, kite\n- step 5: custom shaders: god rays, fog, birds, fireflies and kite string sway\n- step 6: custom shaders: a paint post-pass that turns every frame into brushstrokes\n- step 7: custom shaders: tie the brush style to sun height: gouache by day, oil at sunset\n- step 8: three.js: a camera path along the walk, with the sun setting as you go\n\nwho does what:\n\n> opus 5.5: writes every mesh, shader and camera move\n> three.js: renders the world\n> the paint shader: makes it look like a painting\n> you: judge each frame like a painting, not a game\nthe brushstrokes hide what code-built shapes can’t fake",
